# Test case for ADXL345 accelerometer streaming + resonance testing
# with real firmware sample traffic (sensor_adxl345.c FIFO bursts over
# SPI, 13-bit decode, sensor_bulk reports). REQUIRES_EMULATOR: under
# fileoutput the chip produces no samples, so ACCELEROMETER_QUERY and
# TEST_RESONANCES error by design - there is no upstream fileoutput
# equivalent of this test, so nothing degrades. The bridge streams a
# synthetic 45 Hz x-axis tone (see adxl345.fixture.json), so the
# resonance sweep has a real spectral line to find; the assertions pin
# that samples actually flowed (ACCELEROMETER_QUERY errors with "No
# accelerometer measurements found" and TEST_RESONANCES with
# "measured no data" when they don't).
CONFIG adxl345.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
EMULATOR adxl345.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "accelerometer values"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Resonances data written to"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "measured no data"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "No accelerometer measurements found"

# Home the printer
G28
G1 F6000
G1 X10 Y10 Z10

# Stream raw accelerometer data
ACCELEROMETER_MEASURE CHIP=adxl345 NAME=emu
G4 P1000
ACCELEROMETER_MEASURE CHIP=adxl345 NAME=emu

# Live query (errors if no samples arrived)
ACCELEROMETER_QUERY CHIP=adxl345

# Resonance sweep across the synthetic 45 Hz tone
TEST_RESONANCES AXIS=X FREQ_START=30 FREQ_END=60
